  "explanation": "The question asks 'When was the Goodrich House built?' and requires identifying the construction period of the Goodrich House. Two distinct sources (D1S5 and D2S5) provide conflicting dates—1861–1862 and 1881–1882—for the same Goodrich House in Hudson, Michigan. Both are directly relevant and supported by their respective documents. The third candidate (1850) refers to the Pritchard-Moore-Goodrich House in Griffin, Georgia (D3S3), which is a different structure and location, and thus irrelevant to the question. Therefore, the two valid answers are retained as they represent distinct but valid claims about the same entity."
